# Activity: Web Notifications API & Native Audio Chime Integration

## 1. Objective & Context
Allow Roubit to alert the user even when the browser tab is backgrounded. Integrate the native browser `Notification` API with permission management, plus a subtle chime synthesized via Web Audio API.

- **Prerequisites:** Activity 14.1 (Notification Store).
- **Target Location:** `frontend/src/services/notificationAudio.ts` and `frontend/src/stores/notification.ts`.

## 2. Technical Scope & Specifications
- **Permission Flow:**
  - Provide explicit user action button ("Ativar Notificações do Sistema") in user settings / navbar.
  - Call `Notification.requestPermission()` only upon explicit user gesture.
- **Native OS Notification:**
  - When permission is granted, instantiate `new Notification(title, { body, icon: '/favicon.ico', tag })`.
  - Handle notification click: focus browser window and navigate to the relevant routine block or habit.
- **Web Audio Chime:**
  - Synthesize a subtle two-tone chime (520Hz -> 659Hz) with exponential gain decay.
  - No external mp3/wav assets required.

## 3. Implementation Steps
1. Create `notificationAudio.ts` utility for Web Audio chime synthesis.
2. Add `requestSystemPermission()` action to `useNotificationStore`.
3. Dispatch OS notification on incoming high-priority events when tab is hidden (`document.hidden`).

## 4. Definition of Done (DoD)
- [ ] OS notifications fire when permitted and document is hidden.
- [ ] Subtle chime plays without audio latency.
- [ ] Degrades gracefully when notifications are blocked or unsupported.
